<!-- The Last of Us Remastered, CUSA00552 v01.00, eboot.bin sha256
     c7621501c6e7f1051675cee39549859da9a14c43f29442bd046ed689fa25b323. Author: Iuliia Gailova.
     "Bug Fix - Address Space Base": the engine's memory areas (memory-area-ps4.cpp) take 4 GiB
     slots from a counter in .data that starts at 0x1000000000 (image offset 0x15175a0; the two
     functions at image offsets 0xaa01b0 and 0xaa0290 hand out a slot and add 4 GiB), then map
     direct memory with the slot as a hint and assert that the memory landed there. macOS reserves
     0xfc0000000-0x7000000000 in every process (mmap there fails with EACCES, also MAP_FIXED, and
     under Rosetta 2), so the counter starts at 0x8800000000 instead: the game's own range in
     ps4mac_port (0x88-0xec00000000, below the runtime's placements). The game takes 6 slots at
     start (0x8800000000-0x9fffffffff); its own limit check (slot + 8 GiB below 0xfc00000000)
     stays. The site is found through the code that reads the counter.
     "Resolution Patch - <name>": the render settings' default (image offset 0x9103a0) sets four
     size pairs to 1920x1080 (fields +0x08, +0x18, +0x24, +0x38) and a tile grid of width/8 by
     height/4 (+0x40, +0x44). The patch writes the same instructions with the new size, as the
     engine's own mode switch at image offset 0x9104c0 does for its 1280x720, 1168x657 and
     1024x600 modes. run.py picks the patch from render_resolution in spartanport.ini. -->
